{#- How to use this application's credentials: the token request always, SLC calls when it has SLC. -#}
<h3 class="govuk-heading-s">Get an access token</h3>
<p class="govuk-body">Request a token from Microsoft Entra ID with the OAuth 2.0 client credentials flow:</p>
<pre class="apim-code" id="token-request"><code>POST {{ token.url }}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded</code></pre>
<h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Request body</h4>
<pre class="apim-code" id="token-request-body"><code>grant_type=client_credentials
client_id={{ token.clientId }}
client_secret={{ token.clientSecret }}
scope={{ token.scope }}</code></pre>
<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
  <li>client_id is this application's client ID</li>
  <li>client_secret is the secret you saved when it was created or last regenerated</li>
  <li>scope is the Publisher ID (scope) of the API you are calling</li>
</ul>
<p class="govuk-body">The access_token in the response is the token you send with each call.</p>

{% if slc %}
  <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">Call the Scheduling and Listing Court Schedule API</h3>
  <p class="govuk-body">Send the access token with each request:</p>
  <pre class="apim-code" id="slc-request"><code>GET {{ slc.courtScheduleUrl }}
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code></pre>
  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>&lt;case_urn&gt; is the unique reference number of the case</li>
    <li>&lt;token&gt; is the access token from the step above</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">Find a case URN to try</h3>
  <p class="govuk-body">List the test scenarios to get a case URN to use in the request above:</p>
  <pre class="apim-code" id="scenarios-request"><code>GET {{ slc.scenariosUrl }}
Accept: application/json</code></pre>
{% endif %}